# 9. REDIS INTEGRATION

flowCTRL already has a centralized Redis infrastructure with separate cache and queue instances.

Use the existing infrastructure.

Do not create another Redis client or duplicate Redis architecture.

Potential use cases:

* Cache project catalog responses.
* Cache project details.
* Cache categories and technology filters.
* Cache frequently accessed public tutorial data.
* Reduce repeated database queries.

Requirements:

* Appropriate TTLs.
* Clear cache namespaces.
* Cache invalidation after content updates.
* No cross-user data leakage.
* No caching of sensitive user progress in shared keys.
* Graceful handling of Redis unavailability.

Do not introduce BullMQ jobs unless the feature genuinely requires background processing.

